  "note": "First election on the new wards made by an Order of 1937, which cut Londonderry Corporation from five wards and 40 members to three wards and 20: North and South each two aldermen and six councillors, Waterside one alderman and three councillors. Whole council elected; nominations Thursday 5 May, poll Monday 16 May 1938, results declared 17 May. The Waterside members and the North aldermen were returned unopposed; the Unionists won 12 of the 20 seats (Belfast News-Letter, 6, 17 and 18 May 1938). Returned unopposed."
